<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-12986] Redis mget command is broken</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-12986</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When trying to use the redis layer for ignite, noticed that the data returned by the mget command is inconsistent. Hence the mget command is broken. To demostrate here is an example&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
127.0.0.1:11211&amp;gt; set a 1
OK
127.0.0.1:11211&amp;gt; set b 2
OK
127.0.0.1:11211&amp;gt; set c 3
OK
(0.98s)
127.0.0.1:11211&amp;gt; mget a b c 
1) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;1&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
2) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;2&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
3) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;3&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
127.0.0.1:11211&amp;gt; mget c b a
1) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;1&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
2) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;2&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
3) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;3&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
127.0.0.1:11211&amp;gt; mget a c b
1) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;1&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
2) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;2&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
3) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;3&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you notice, the order of the values returned does not match the order of the values returned.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In order to demonstrate the expected behaviour, will run the same commands against a real redis instance and paste the output below.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
127.0.0.1:6379&amp;gt; set a 1 
OK
127.0.0.1:6379&amp;gt; set b 2 
OK
127.0.0.1:6379&amp;gt; set c 3
OK
127.0.0.1:6379&amp;gt; mget a b c 
1) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;1&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
2) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;2&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
3) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;3&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
127.0.0.1:6379&amp;gt; mget c b a
1) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;3&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
2) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;2&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
3) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;1&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
127.0.0.1:6379&amp;gt; mget a c b
1) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;1&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
2) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;3&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
3) &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;2&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is not only happening on the redis-cli, it is also happening when using redis client libraries. &lt;/p&gt;</description>
